// The desktop's own words: its menu items, its windows' names, and its alerts' button.
// The desktop asks for each by its key, so keep the keys and change the text. A key
// that's missing shows as 101:key, and the desktop reports it. %s is filled in, such
// as the app's name in "Quit %s".

// The standard menus' titles.
file ^File^
edit ^Edit^
view ^View^
help ^Help^

// File and Edit's own items.
closeWindow ^Close Window^
undo ^Undo^
redo ^Redo^
cut ^Cut^
copy ^Copy^
paste ^Paste^
selectAll ^Select All^

// The VentureOS menu, Help when no app is in front, and About's window.
aboutSystem ^About VentureOS^
returnToShell ^Return to Shell^
aboutApp ^About %s^
version ^Version %s^

// An app's menu.
newWindow ^New Window^
quitApp ^Quit %s^

// Alerts.
ok ^OK^

// Quick Look: a file's kind, size, and an app's details.
quickLookFolder ^Folder^
quickLookFile ^File^
quickLookApp ^Application^
quickLookBrokenApp ^Application that can't open^
quickLookBrokenInterface ^Interface that can't be shown^
quickLookNoVersion ^not given^
quickLookNeeds ^Needs %s^
quickLookShowingFirst ^(Showing the first %s of %s.)^
oneItem ^1 item^
items ^%s items^
oneByte ^1 byte^
bytes ^%s bytes^
kilobytes ^%s KB^
megabytes ^%s MB^

// vdb's question when a computer asks to send apps.
trustTitle ^Trust This Computer?^
trust ^Trust^
deny ^Deny^
